WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were talking backstage.
You did a great job

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
delivering
the Democratic response

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the State of the Union.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.572 line:92%
-That has often been fraught,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether it's a Republican
delivering it

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
or a Democrat
delivering a response.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:13.346
Like, Marco Rubio, for example,
had to keep drinking water.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you prepare
for this moment?

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hydrated well and early.
-Okay.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I used a moisturizing
but not glistening lipstick.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.458
-I practiced wandering in
like I knew where I was

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.395 size:84% position:42%
and not like I was just
walking off the stage.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.965 line:92%
And I prayed really hard.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.167 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And in that moment --

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.935 line:92%
Because I imagine that is --

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
When it starts is
when you realize

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
exactly how well-prepared
you are for it.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.409
Did you feel as though --
good about the moment?

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:47.147
-So, we decided to make certain
I said "happy Lunar New Year"

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was
the Lunar New Year.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.853
That's a hard word to say if
you haven't practiced it before.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah -- Lunar New Year.
-Yes.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, trying to say
"happy Lunar New Year"

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:01.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a shot clock
and when you've over-hydrated,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's really bad.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I practiced it,
it sounded mangled.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was awful.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I really was like,
"Please, God,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.604 size:84% position:42%
just say this properly,
and you'll be okay."

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
And once that was done,
I'm like, "Cool.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump, whatever."
-Nice job.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.877 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Very, very nice job.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:22.882
Moving on to the name
you just mentioned, you were --

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm sorry.
-That's all right.
We bring him up, too.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.254 line:92%
It sounds like he's going to

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
declare a national emergency
over this border wall.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.460 size:88% position:44%
I guess, to some degree,
we can't be surprised.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.797 size:88% position:44%
But what is your sort of
first reaction to this?

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think
laughter's appropriate, but...

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.136 line:92%
Yeah, actually, laughter.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:48.908
-I think he realizes he was
outmatched by Nancy Pelosi,

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that he received --

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.178 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.747 size:78% position:39%
That he got less than
he would have gotten

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.616 line:92%
had he not had a temper tantrum.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:02:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
But more than anything,
it's not real.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.489 size:81% position:41% line:92%
There is no emergency.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is not national.
It is in his head.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he will be sued
so many times.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.396
But what he's
looking forward to --
and I think we will give him --

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that we will have
a histrionic fit about this,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.501 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and then we'll realize

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just like everything else
he hasn't done.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why are we reacting
to yet another untruth?

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So would your advice be,
then...

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.412 size:78% position:39% line:92%
...to just ignore it?

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because obviously, you want to
bring legal challenges,

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would seem.
-Oh, we should sue him,
of course.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely.
Because left unchecked,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
he will declare
a national emergency

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
because tanning beds are
disappearing from the shelves.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.260 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. Yeah.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.329 size:88% position:44%
-But in all seriousness,
I do think there is --

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:47.433
there is necessary response,
but it doesn't have to be public

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it doesn't
have to be constant.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.839
We validate his behavior
by treating it as serious.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
What we should treat it as
is fraudulent

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.510 line:92%
and fraught with egotism,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that means sue him,
let him lose,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
and don't give him the
credibility of treating this
as serious.

